WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
The family business.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Before dad died, he told me something.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Something about you.
What's did he tell you?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
He said that I might
have to kill you, Sam.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
I don't know.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Did he know the demon's plans for me?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Am I supposed to go
dark side or something?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Who are you? Please.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
You're in danger.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
What's your name? Ava Wilson.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
You must be one of us. One of who?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
One of the psychics like me.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
There are others like us out there,

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
And we're all part of something.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
I'm not part of anything, okay?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Do you see this?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
I am getting married in eight weeks.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
You can't run from this,

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
And you can't protect me.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
I can try.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Maybe I can help.
You've done all you can.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Just go back to your
fianc. You'll be safe there.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Promise me you'll call, then.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
I promise.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Ava...

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Most of the stuff is up here.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Still can't believe
you're closing this house.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
My parents got engaged here.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.475
My grandparents too.

00:00:00.582 --> 00:00:02.475
Yeah, a lot of people did.

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.405
Boxes are at the end of
the hall. Need any help?

00:00:05.473 --> 00:00:06.795
No, ma'am. I got it.

00:00:13.342 --> 00:00:15.456
He's gonna take our toys?

00:00:15.913 --> 00:00:17.895
Only the ones you
don't play with anymore.

00:00:18.403 --> 00:00:20.438
It's not like you don't
have enough already.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.667
Son of a bitch. Son of a bitch.

00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:25.075
Watch your mouth.

00:00:25.132 --> 00:00:26.576
Maggie said it first.

00:00:26.661 --> 00:00:28.106
Watch your mouth too, Maggie.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:07.678
Good night, Tabitha.

00:01:39.503 --> 00:01:41.176
Oh my god! Yes, yes are you there?

00:01:41.182 --> 00:01:43.377
Please you have to send someone now.

00:01:44.421 --> 00:01:45.548
There's been an accident.

00:01:45.551 --> 00:01:48.588
A man fell down my stairs,
and I don't know if he's...

00:01:48.623 --> 00:01:51.157
His head is like
completely turned around.

00:01:52.331 --> 00:01:54.775
Tyler, don't look! Don't look!

00:01:55.251 --> 00:01:56.207
Oh yes, yes!

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.447
As soon as possible.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.518
Just hurry, please hurry!

00:02:04.832 --> 00:02:07.477
I don't know, I didn't
see how it happened.

00:02:22.051 --> 00:02:23.257
Yeah.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.117
Okay. Thanks, Ellen.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.156
What did she have to
say? She got nothing.

00:02:30.621 --> 00:02:32.767
Me, I've been checking every
database I can think of,

00:02:32.833 --> 00:02:34.328
Federal, state, and local.

00:02:34.411 --> 00:02:36.646
No one's heard anything
about Ava. She's just...

00:02:36.691 --> 00:02:38.385
Into thin air, you know?

00:02:39.282 --> 00:02:40.426
What about you?

00:02:40.513 --> 00:02:43.176
No, same as before. Sorry, man.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.178
Ellen did have one thing.

00:02:46.953 --> 00:02:49.277
A hotel in Cornwall, Connecticut,

00:02:49.351 --> 00:02:51.448
Two freak accidents in
the past three weeks.

00:02:51.492 --> 00:02:53.167
Yeah, what's that have to do with Ava?

00:02:53.572 --> 00:02:54.837
It's a job.

00:02:54.842 --> 00:02:56.745
I mean, a lady drowned in the bathtub,

00:02:56.782 --> 00:02:58.928
Then a few days ago, a
guy falls down the stairs,

00:02:58.973 --> 00:03:00.475
Head turns a complete 180,

00:03:00.481 --> 00:03:02.446
Which isn't exactly normal, you know?

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.447
Look, I don't know,
Dean, it might be nothing,

00:03:04.451 --> 00:03:06.668
But I told Ellen we'd
think about checking it out.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:08.637
You did? Yeah.

00:03:11.051 --> 00:03:13.466
You seem surprised. Yeah,
it's just, you know...

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.967
Not the patented Sam
Winchester way, is it?

00:03:17.522 --> 00:03:18.895
What way is that?

00:03:18.973 --> 00:03:21.848
Just figured after Ava,
there'd be, you know, more

00:03:21.932 --> 00:03:26.398
Angst and droopy music and
staring out the rainy windows.

00:03:28.423 --> 00:03:30.007
I'll shut up now.

00:03:30.253 --> 00:03:31.276
Look,

00:03:31.281 --> 00:03:33.598
I'm the one who told
her to go back home.

00:03:34.411 --> 00:03:36.346
Now her fianc's dead,

00:03:36.372 --> 00:03:39.335
And some demon has taken
her off to god knows where,

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:40.628
You know?

00:03:41.893 --> 00:03:43.617
We've been looking for a month now,

00:03:44.262 --> 00:03:45.726
And we got nothing.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:48.858
So I'm not giving up on her, but

00:03:48.863 --> 00:03:51.018
I'm not gonna let
other people die either.

00:03:52.262 --> 00:03:54.598
We got to save as many people as we can.

00:03:56.891 --> 00:03:59.956
Wow, that attitude is just
way too healthy for me.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.698
I'm officially
uncomfortable now. Thank you.

00:04:05.853 --> 00:04:07.786
All right, call Ellen.
Tell her we'll take it.

00:04:21.871 --> 00:04:23.915
Dude, this is sweet.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.488
I never get to work jobs like this.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.286
Like what?

00:04:28.792 --> 00:04:31.176
Old-School haunted houses. You know,

00:04:31.563 --> 00:04:34.306
Fog, secret passage ways,

00:04:34.311 --> 00:04:36.378
Sissy  british accents.

00:04:37.051 --> 00:04:39.697
Might even run into Fred and
Daphne while we're inside.

00:04:41.911 --> 00:04:43.987
Daphne... Love her.

00:04:47.463 --> 00:04:48.858
Hey, wait a sec.

00:04:50.263 --> 00:04:52.688
I'm not so sure haunted's the problem.

00:04:52.782 --> 00:04:53.866
What do you mean?

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:56.108
You see this pattern here?

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:59.785
That's a quincunx. It's a five-Spot.

00:05:00.432 --> 00:05:02.236
Five-Spot. Yeah.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.736
That's for hoodoo spellwork, isn't it?

00:05:03.742 --> 00:05:05.406
Right. Hey, you fill
this thing with bloodweed,

00:05:05.532 --> 00:05:07.516
You got a powerful charm
to ward off enemies.

00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:09.216
Except I don't see any bloodweed.

00:05:09.343 --> 00:05:11.298
Don't you think this
place is a little too

00:05:11.863 --> 00:05:13.435
White-Meat for hoodoo?

00:05:15.292 --> 00:05:16.447
Maybe.

00:05:22.372 --> 00:05:23.518
May I help you?

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:26.488
Hi. Yeah, I'd like a room
for a couple of nights.

00:05:27.763 --> 00:05:28.638
Hey!

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:31.786
Sorry about that. No problem.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:35.417
Well, congratulations. You could
be some of our final guests.

00:05:35.481 --> 00:05:37.816
Well, sounds vaguely ominous.

00:05:37.852 --> 00:05:40.665
No, I'm sorry. I mean, we're
closing at the end of the month.

00:05:41.683 --> 00:05:44.176
Let me guess. You guys
are here antiquing?

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.497
How'd you know? You just look the type.

00:05:48.583 --> 00:05:50.367
So, a king-Size bed?

00:05:50.693 --> 00:05:52.727
What? No. No, no.

00:05:53.863 --> 00:05:56.455
Two singles. We're just brothers.

00:05:56.891 --> 00:05:59.808
Oh. Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:04.335
What did you mean that
we looked the type?

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.108
You know,

00:06:07.122 --> 00:06:10.025
Speaking of antiques, you have a really

00:06:10.031 --> 00:06:11.997
Interesting urn on the front porch.

00:06:12.062 --> 00:06:13.957
Where did you get that?
You know, I have no idea.

00:06:13.962 --> 00:06:15.085
It's been there forever.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.425
Here you go, Mr. Mahogoff.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:20.997
You'll be staying in room 237.

00:06:21.863 --> 00:06:24.186
Sherwin, could you show these
gentlemen to their rooms?

00:06:25.383 --> 00:06:26.488
Let me guess...

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.355
Antiquers?

00:06:30.661 --> 00:06:32.345
I can give you a hand with that bag.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:33.895
I got it. Okay.

00:06:34.811 --> 00:06:36.405
So the hotel's closing up, huh?

00:06:36.405 --> 00:06:39.064
Yep. Miss Susan tried
to make a go of it,

00:06:39.147 --> 00:06:41.196
But the guests just don't
come like they used to.

00:06:41.352 --> 00:06:43.723
Still, it's a damn shame. Oh yeah?

00:06:43.754 --> 00:06:47.508
It may not look it anymore,
but this place was a palace.

00:06:47.571 --> 00:06:50.627
Two different vice-Presidents
laid their heads on our pillows.

00:06:50.891 --> 00:06:54.297
My parents worked here. I
practically grew up here.

00:06:54.752 --> 00:06:56.055
I'm gonna miss it.

00:06:56.923 --> 00:06:58.147
Here's your room.

00:07:04.243 --> 00:07:05.177
Thanks.

00:07:12.903 --> 00:07:15.486
You're not gonna cheap
out on me, are you, boy?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:25.884
What the...

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:27.906
What?

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:29.828
That's normal.

00:07:30.903 --> 00:07:32.754
Why the hell would anyone stay here?

00:07:32.762 --> 00:07:34.686
I'm amazed they kept
in business this long.

00:07:36.152 --> 00:07:39.728
All right, victim number one,
Joan Edison, 43 years old,

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:42.216
A realtor handling
the sale of the hotel.

00:07:42.259 --> 00:07:45.397
And victim number two
was Larry Williams,

00:07:45.401 --> 00:07:47.215
Moving some stuff out to goodwill.

00:07:47.281 --> 00:07:49.378
Well, there's a connexion. They're
both tied up in shutting the place down.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.384
Yeah, maybe someone here
doesn't want to leave,

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:53.016
And they're using hoodoo to fight back.

00:07:53.111 --> 00:07:55.115
Who do you think our witch
doctor is. This Susan lady?

00:07:55.221 --> 00:07:56.427
Doesn't seem likely.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.108
I mean, she's the one selling.

00:07:58.181 --> 00:07:59.528
So, what then, Sherwin?

00:08:01.033 --> 00:08:02.387
I don't know.

00:08:03.333 --> 00:08:05.046
Of course, the most
troubling question is,

00:08:05.052 --> 00:08:06.775
Why do these people assume we're gay?

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.177
You are kind of butch.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:10.495
Probably think you're over compensating.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:13.175
Right.

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:30.086
Hey.

00:08:31.831 --> 00:08:34.217
Look at that. More hoodoo.

00:08:47.312 --> 00:08:48.905
Hi, there. Hi.

00:08:48.923 --> 00:08:50.268
Everything  okay with your room?

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:51.617
Yeah, yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:08:51.692 --> 00:08:53.375
Yeah, everything's great. Good.

00:08:57.362 --> 00:09:00.238
Well, I was just in the
middle of packing. So...

00:09:00.312 --> 00:09:03.697
Hey, are those antique dolls?

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.088
'Cause this one, this one here,

00:09:06.093 --> 00:09:08.238
He's got a major doll
collection back home.

00:09:08.242 --> 00:09:09.748
Don't you? Huh?

00:09:12.912 --> 00:09:15.256
Big time. Big time.

00:09:15.352 --> 00:09:18.098
You think he could come in, well,
we could come in and take a look?

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:21.237
I don't know. Please?
I mean, he loves them.

00:09:21.331 --> 00:09:22.295
He's not gonna tell you this,

00:09:22.302 --> 00:09:24.455
But he's always dressing them
up in little tiny outfits.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:27.754
You'd make his day. She would. Huh? Huh?

00:09:29.271 --> 00:09:30.416
It's true.

00:09:31.942 --> 00:09:33.965
Okay. Come on in. All right.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.145
All right!

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:41.848
Wow.

00:09:42.831 --> 00:09:44.767
This is a lot of dolls.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:48.504
They're nice, you know.
They're not supercreepy at all.

00:09:49.201 --> 00:09:51.818
I suppose they are a little creepy.

00:09:51.863 --> 00:09:53.506
But they've been in the family forever.

00:09:53.523 --> 00:09:55.877
A lot of sentimental
value. What is this?

00:09:56.373 --> 00:09:58.128
The hotel? Yeah, that's right.

00:09:58.153 --> 00:09:59.706
Exact replica, custom-Built.

00:10:07.871 --> 00:10:09.485
His head got twisted around.

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:12.996
What happened to it?

00:10:13.061 --> 00:10:14.487
Tyler, probably.

00:10:14.562 --> 00:10:15.798
Mommy.

00:10:16.983 --> 00:10:18.708
Maggie's being mean.

00:10:18.801 --> 00:10:21.138
Tyler, tell her I said to be nice, okay?

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:24.475
Hey, Tyler. I see you broke
your doll. You want me to fix it?

00:10:24.542 --> 00:10:27.816
I didn't break it. I found it like that.

00:10:28.301 --> 00:10:32.198
Well, maybe Maggie did it.
No, neither of us did it.

00:10:32.211 --> 00:10:34.078
Grandma would get mad if we broke him.

00:10:34.171 --> 00:10:36.295
Tyler, she wouldn't get mad. Grandma?

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:39.884
Grandma Rose. These were all her toys.

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:41.767
Oh, really?

00:10:42.129 --> 00:10:43.826
Where's grandma Rose now?

00:10:44.061 --> 00:10:45.496
Up in her room.

00:10:45.883 --> 00:10:48.916
You know, I'd really
love to talk to Rose

00:10:48.921 --> 00:10:50.725
About her incredible doll... No.

00:10:53.391 --> 00:10:54.575
I  mean,

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:56.406
I'm  afraid that's impossible.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:00.096
My mother's been very sick, and
she's not taking any visitors.

00:11:05.421 --> 00:11:06.945
What do you think?

00:11:07.033 --> 00:11:08.455
Dolls, hoodoo,

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:10.435
Mysterious shut-In grandma?

00:11:10.463 --> 00:11:13.878
Well, dolls are used in all
kind of voodoo and hoodoo,

00:11:13.912 --> 00:11:16.646
Like curses and binding spells.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:18.715
Yeah, maybe we found our witch doctor.

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:21.068
I'll go see what I can dig upon granny.

00:11:21.072 --> 00:11:23.698
You get online, check old obits,
freak accidents. That sort of things.

00:11:23.732 --> 00:11:25.754
See if she's whacked
anybody before. Right.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:28.295
Don't go surfing porn. It's
not the kind of whacking I mean.

00:11:33.831 --> 00:11:35.448
I've been meaning to ask...

00:11:35.451 --> 00:11:37.427
What sort of renovations
are you planning?

00:11:37.503 --> 00:11:38.795
They never told you?

00:11:38.802 --> 00:11:40.297
Told me what?

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:43.228
Miss Thompson, we plan
on demolishing the hotel.

00:11:44.223 --> 00:11:46.495
Oh. I see.

00:11:47.753 --> 00:11:49.057
Excuse me.

00:13:14.791 --> 00:13:15.865
What happened?

00:13:16.552 --> 00:13:20.336
The maid went into turn down
the sheets, and he was just

00:13:20.821 --> 00:13:23.037
Hanging there. That's awful.

00:13:23.043 --> 00:13:24.358
He was a guest?

00:13:24.401 --> 00:13:26.315
He worked for the company
that bought the place.

00:13:28.772 --> 00:13:31.257
I don't understand. What?

00:13:31.281 --> 00:13:33.747
Had a lot of bad luck around here.

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:37.718
Look, if you'd like to check
out, I'll give you a full refund.

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:40.288
No, thanks. I don't scare that easy.

00:13:48.822 --> 00:13:50.198
There's been another one.

00:13:50.201 --> 00:13:51.998
Some guy just hung himself in his room.

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:54.826
Yeah. I saw.

00:13:54.891 --> 00:13:56.427
We got figure this out and fast.

00:13:56.781 --> 00:13:58.317
What did you find out about granny?

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:01.475
You're bossy.

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:04.198
What?

00:14:05.421 --> 00:14:07.045
You're bossy.

00:14:08.271 --> 00:14:09.467
You're short.

00:14:10.661 --> 00:14:12.617
Are you drunk? Yeah.

00:14:13.403 --> 00:14:14.485
So?

00:14:14.802 --> 00:14:16.006
Stupid.

00:14:17.841 --> 00:14:19.798
Dude, what are you thinking?
We're working a case.

00:14:23.392 --> 00:14:26.367
That guy who hung himself...

00:14:28.701 --> 00:14:30.588
I couldn't save him. What
are you talking about?

00:14:30.661 --> 00:14:31.858
You didn't know. You
couldn't have done anything.

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:33.485
That's an excuse, Dean.

00:14:34.942 --> 00:14:37.235
I should have found a way to save him.

00:14:38.792 --> 00:14:40.777
I should have saved Ava too.

00:14:41.252 --> 00:14:43.627
Well, you can't save
everyone. Even you said that.

00:14:43.721 --> 00:14:45.745
No, Dean, you don't
understand, all right?

00:14:45.759 --> 00:14:48.415
The more people I save,
the more I can change.

00:14:48.491 --> 00:14:51.027
Change what? My destiny, Dean.

00:14:53.591 --> 00:14:55.805
All right, time for
bed. Come on, sasquatch.

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:56.826
Come on.

00:14:56.911 --> 00:14:59.465
I need you to watch out
for me. Yeah, I always do.

00:14:59.561 --> 00:15:02.585
No. No, no, no. You have
to watch out for me...

00:15:03.352 --> 00:15:04.725
All right?

00:15:05.259 --> 00:15:08.456
And if I ever turn into
something that I'm not...

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.256
You have to kill me. Sam...

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:15.716
Dean, dad told you
to do it. You have to.

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:18.307
Yeah, well, dad's an ass.

00:15:18.682 --> 00:15:20.677
He never should have said
anything. I mean, you don't do that.

00:15:20.692 --> 00:15:22.515
You don't lay that
kinda crap on your kids.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:24.656
No, he was right to say it.

00:15:25.163 --> 00:15:27.336
Who knows what I might become?

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.918
Even now, everyone around me dies.

00:15:30.009 --> 00:15:32.394
Well, I'm not dying, okay?

00:15:32.482 --> 00:15:34.077
And neither are you. Come on, sit down.

00:15:34.352 --> 00:15:37.875
No, please, Dean, you're
the only one who can do it.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:39.968
Promise me. Don't ask that of me.

00:15:40.043 --> 00:15:41.298
Dean, please.

00:15:41.302 --> 00:15:43.184
You have to promise me.

00:15:49.091 --> 00:15:50.444
I promise.

00:15:53.631 --> 00:15:54.966
Thanks.

00:15:57.759 --> 00:15:59.205
Thank you...

00:16:40.782 --> 00:16:42.346
Find any good antiques?

00:16:42.951 --> 00:16:46.077
No, no. Got distracted.

00:16:46.722 --> 00:16:47.787
Have a drink.

00:16:47.981 --> 00:16:49.597
Yeah, thanks.

00:16:53.771 --> 00:16:57.227
So, poor guy, huh, killing himself?

00:16:58.423 --> 00:17:01.388
That kind of thing seems
to be going around lately.

00:17:01.461 --> 00:17:03.944
Yeah. Yeah, I heard
about the other ones.

00:17:04.032 --> 00:17:07.567
It's almost like this hotel
is cursed or something.

00:17:07.569 --> 00:17:10.245
Every hotel has its spilled blood.

00:17:11.813 --> 00:17:13.436
If people only knew what's going on

00:17:13.441 --> 00:17:15.615
In some of those rooms
they've checked into.

00:17:17.701 --> 00:17:19.575
You know a lot about
the place, don't you?

00:17:19.603 --> 00:17:21.388
Down to the last nail.

00:17:22.162 --> 00:17:24.008
I'd love to hear some stories.

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:26.158
Boy,

00:17:26.563 --> 00:17:29.105
You should never say that to an old man.

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:36.466
This is little miss Susan
and her mother, Rose.

00:17:36.833 --> 00:17:38.345
Happier days.

00:17:41.792 --> 00:17:43.434
They're not happy now?

00:17:43.813 --> 00:17:47.417
Well, would you be, leaving
the only home you ever knew?

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:50.007
I don't know. I never really knew one.

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:52.026
Well, this is Rose's home.

00:17:52.032 --> 00:17:54.126
Been in the family over a century.

00:17:54.201 --> 00:17:56.295
Used to be the family estate,

00:17:56.303 --> 00:17:59.888
And now she gets to live in
some senior-Living graveyard,

00:17:59.923 --> 00:18:01.987
And they tear this place down.

00:18:03.082 --> 00:18:04.674
That's too bad.

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:08.587
I hear Rose isn't feeling well either.

00:18:08.593 --> 00:18:09.765
No, she isn't.

00:18:10.312 --> 00:18:11.408
What's wrong with her?

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:13.757
It's not my business to say.

00:18:18.891 --> 00:18:20.525
Who's this?

00:18:21.292 --> 00:18:23.036
That's Rose

00:18:24.069 --> 00:18:25.638
When she was a little girl.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:34.845
Who's that with her?

00:18:34.952 --> 00:18:36.665
That's her nanny, Marie.

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:39.317
She looked after Rose
more than her own mother.

00:19:02.111 --> 00:19:03.737
How you feeling, Sammy?

00:19:05.311 --> 00:19:09.095
I guess mixing whiskey and jager
wasn't such a gangbuster idea, was it?

00:19:11.671 --> 00:19:14.335
I'll bet you don't remember a
thing from last night, do you?

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:16.617
No, I can still taste the tequila.

00:19:18.321 --> 00:19:20.776
You know, there's a really
good hangover remedy. It's uh...

00:19:20.862 --> 00:19:24.467
It's a greasy pork sandwich
served up in a dirty ashtray.

00:19:24.511 --> 00:19:26.365
Oh, I hate you. I know you do.

00:19:27.771 --> 00:19:30.148
Hey, turns out when
grandma Rose was a tyke,

00:19:30.799 --> 00:19:34.097
She had a creole nanny
who wore a hoodoo necklace.

00:19:35.741 --> 00:19:38.296
So you think she taught
Rose hoodoo? Yes, I do.

00:19:40.561 --> 00:19:41.595
All right.

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:45.934
I think it's time we talk to Rose, then.

00:19:46.039 --> 00:19:47.986
Oh, you need to brush your teeth first.

00:19:58.211 --> 00:19:59.307
Hello?

00:20:00.701 --> 00:20:02.076
Susan?

00:20:03.821 --> 00:20:04.857
Clear?

00:21:29.823 --> 00:21:31.378
Mrs. Thompson?

00:21:35.009 --> 00:21:36.698
Mrs. Thompson?

00:21:39.731 --> 00:21:40.956
Rose?

00:21:44.143 --> 00:21:47.477
Hi, Mrs. Thompson. We're not
here to hurt you. It's okay. We...

00:21:51.413 --> 00:21:52.737
Rose?

00:21:58.260 --> 00:21:59.017
Dean.

00:22:02.772 --> 00:22:04.545
This woman's had a stroke.

00:22:05.822 --> 00:22:07.817
Yeah, but hoodoo's hands-On. Yeah.

00:22:07.822 --> 00:22:10.436
You got to mix herbs and
chant, build an altar.

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:12.347
So it can't be Rose.

00:22:12.383 --> 00:22:15.246
Hey, maybe it's not even hoodoo.
You know, she could be faking.

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:17.086
What do you want to do,
poke her with a stick?

00:22:18.292 --> 00:22:20.236
Dude, you're not gonna
poke her with a stick.

00:22:20.319 --> 00:22:21.676
What the hell?

00:22:21.722 --> 00:22:23.246
What are you doing in here?

00:22:23.572 --> 00:22:25.186
We just wanted to talk to Rose.

00:22:25.222 --> 00:22:27.057
Look at her. She's
scared out of her wits.

00:22:27.153 --> 00:22:29.235
I want you out of my
hotel in two minutes

00:22:29.242 --> 00:22:30.485
Or I'm calling the cops.

00:22:47.601 --> 00:22:49.625
Your turn. Eightsies.

00:22:56.313 --> 00:22:57.947
Have you started packing yet?

00:22:57.961 --> 00:22:59.567
No. Why not?

00:22:59.642 --> 00:23:00.996
I don't want to move.

00:23:01.059 --> 00:23:03.517
Yes, I know, but we have to.

00:23:03.540 --> 00:23:05.615
But Maggie says we're
not allowed to move.

00:23:05.660 --> 00:23:06.507
Yeah?

00:23:07.143 --> 00:23:10.946
Tyler, enough. Maggie is imaginary.

00:23:10.992 --> 00:23:14.105
You're too old to have an imaginary
friend, and I am done pretending.

00:23:18.211 --> 00:23:19.857
I don't like her.

00:23:41.201 --> 00:23:43.067
I  could lug those boxes for you.

00:23:43.071 --> 00:23:44.956
I got it, Sherwin. Thanks.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:46.346
Okay, then.

00:23:46.823 --> 00:23:48.116
See you later.

00:25:53.313 --> 00:25:55.585
You okay? I think so.

00:25:56.530 --> 00:25:58.418
Come on. Come on. Let's
get inside. Let's go.

00:26:02.123 --> 00:26:04.476
Whiskey. Sure.

00:26:04.510 --> 00:26:05.996
I know the feeling.

00:26:07.682 --> 00:26:09.548
What the hell happened out there?

00:26:10.313 --> 00:26:12.018
You want the truth? Of course.

00:26:12.080 --> 00:26:14.285
At first, we thought it was
some sort of a hoodoo curse,

00:26:14.750 --> 00:26:15.975
But that out there...

00:26:16.412 --> 00:26:18.225
That was definitely a spirit.

00:26:18.782 --> 00:26:19.948
Here.

00:26:20.740 --> 00:26:22.267
You're insane.

00:26:23.081 --> 00:26:24.277
It's been said.

00:26:24.301 --> 00:26:25.466
Look, I'm sorry, Susan.

00:26:25.472 --> 00:26:27.607
We don't exactly have
time to ease you into this,

00:26:27.642 --> 00:26:29.865
But we need to know when
your mother had the stroke.

00:26:30.250 --> 00:26:32.926
What does that have to do...
Just answer the question.

00:26:33.711 --> 00:26:35.028
About a month ago.

00:26:35.240 --> 00:26:36.976
Right before the killings began.

00:26:36.980 --> 00:26:38.256
You see?

00:26:38.333 --> 00:26:41.807
So what if Rose was working hoodoo,
but not to hurt anyone, to protect them?

00:26:41.913 --> 00:26:44.168
She was using the urn patterns
to ward off the spirit.

00:26:44.230 --> 00:26:46.027
Right. Until she had a
stroke and couldn't anymore.

00:26:46.040 --> 00:26:47.446
I don't believe this. Listen,

00:26:47.480 --> 00:26:50.076
That car didn't try to run
you down by itself, okay?

00:26:50.932 --> 00:26:54.336
I mean, I guess it did technically,
but with a spirit. Forget it.

00:26:54.340 --> 00:26:55.487
Just believe what you want, alright?

00:26:55.539 --> 00:26:57.616
But the fact is you and
your family are in danger.

00:26:57.712 --> 00:26:59.696
So you need to clear
everybody out of here.

00:26:59.772 --> 00:27:01.105
Your employees,

00:27:01.111 --> 00:27:02.184
Your mother,

00:27:02.192 --> 00:27:03.917
Your daughters, everyone.

00:27:06.290 --> 00:27:09.516
I only have one daughter. One?

00:27:09.559 --> 00:27:11.248
I thought Tyler had
a sister named Maggie.

00:27:12.280 --> 00:27:13.995
Maggie's imaginary.

00:27:16.613 --> 00:27:17.686
Where's Tyler?

00:27:23.672 --> 00:27:26.037
She's going to stay here with me,

00:27:26.732 --> 00:27:28.707
And you can't stop me.

00:27:29.172 --> 00:27:32.388
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:27:34.773 --> 00:27:37.605
Maggie, don't. You're not
supposed to bother grandma.

00:27:38.323 --> 00:27:39.165
I know.

00:27:41.292 --> 00:27:42.527
Come on.

00:27:43.603 --> 00:27:45.075
Let's play.

00:27:45.593 --> 00:27:47.548
Can we have a tea party?

00:28:02.513 --> 00:28:03.658
Tyler!

00:28:07.941 --> 00:28:10.585
Oh, my god! Tyler!

00:28:15.032 --> 00:28:16.478
She's not here!

00:28:18.819 --> 00:28:19.827
Susan,

00:28:20.252 --> 00:28:22.325
Tell us what you know
about Maggie. Not much.

00:28:22.403 --> 00:28:24.427
Tyler's been talking about
her since mom got sick.

00:28:24.471 --> 00:28:26.077
Okay, did you ever know
anyone by that name?

00:28:26.080 --> 00:28:27.396
Uh no. Think, think.

00:28:27.422 --> 00:28:29.605
Somebody that could have lived
here, might have passed away.

00:28:30.039 --> 00:28:32.708
My god... My mom had
a sister named Margaret.

00:28:32.742 --> 00:28:33.775
She barely spoke about her.

00:28:33.783 --> 00:28:35.664
Did Margaret die here
when she was a kid?

00:28:35.753 --> 00:28:37.538
Yeah, she drowned in the pool.

00:28:38.450 --> 00:28:39.376
Come on.

00:28:58.740 --> 00:29:00.468
I don't like it up here.

00:29:00.471 --> 00:29:02.206
I'm scared.

00:29:02.311 --> 00:29:03.904
It's okay.

00:29:03.911 --> 00:29:05.846
All you have to do is jump.

00:29:08.759 --> 00:29:10.518
I can't swim.

00:29:10.602 --> 00:29:11.706
I know.

00:29:12.230 --> 00:29:13.676
But it won't hurt.

00:29:13.701 --> 00:29:14.875
I promise.

00:29:14.950 --> 00:29:18.126
And then we can be together forever,

00:29:18.132 --> 00:29:20.486
And no one will bother us.

00:29:24.941 --> 00:29:27.428
Why don't you just
come with me and mommy?

00:29:27.503 --> 00:29:31.186
Because I can't leave here,
and you can't leave me.

00:29:34.823 --> 00:29:36.238
Please.

00:29:36.261 --> 00:29:37.944
I don't want to be alone.

00:29:51.799 --> 00:29:53.027
Tyler!

00:29:58.082 --> 00:29:59.286
Mommy!

00:30:05.543 --> 00:30:06.786
Is there another entrance?

00:30:06.840 --> 00:30:08.485
Around back. All right, let's go!

00:30:08.540 --> 00:30:09.458
Keep working.

00:30:34.309 --> 00:30:36.394
It'll all be over soon.

00:30:38.303 --> 00:30:39.257
Stand back.

00:30:42.269 --> 00:30:43.878
Son of a bitch.

00:30:50.751 --> 00:30:52.275
Margaret...

00:30:54.799 --> 00:30:56.856
Margaret...

00:32:00.583 --> 00:32:02.076
Oh, thank god. Thank god!

00:32:02.523 --> 00:32:03.625
Mommy?

00:32:03.690 --> 00:32:05.158
Yeah, baby, I'm here.

00:32:05.790 --> 00:32:08.336
Tyler, do you see Maggie anywhere?

00:32:09.840 --> 00:32:11.355
No, she's gone.

00:32:24.279 --> 00:32:26.126
You'd really do that for me?

00:32:32.790 --> 00:32:34.216
Yes...

00:32:34.290 --> 00:32:35.736
If you did,

00:32:36.241 --> 00:32:37.774
I'd let them go.

00:32:40.002 --> 00:32:41.877
But I don't understand.

00:32:41.919 --> 00:32:44.788
You kept me away for so long.

00:32:45.571 --> 00:32:48.134
I thought you didn't love me anymore.

00:32:52.701 --> 00:32:53.935
Okay...

00:32:54.560 --> 00:32:56.015
Little sister.

00:33:10.941 --> 00:33:12.705
Don't worry, honey. We're
leaving in two minutes.

00:33:12.801 --> 00:33:13.935
We just got to get grandma.

00:33:17.210 --> 00:33:18.888
I don't get it. Did Maggie just stop?

00:33:20.439 --> 00:33:22.727
Seems like it. Where
the hell did she go?

00:33:51.761 --> 00:33:53.765
Paramedics said it was another stroke.

00:33:54.801 --> 00:33:55.826
Do you think...

00:33:56.350 --> 00:33:58.627
Margaret could have had
something to do with it?

00:33:59.292 --> 00:34:00.366
We don't know.

00:34:00.462 --> 00:34:01.785
But it's possible,

00:34:01.792 --> 00:34:02.984
Yeah.

00:34:05.700 --> 00:34:07.326
Susan, I'm sorry.

00:34:07.863 --> 00:34:10.077
You have nothing to apologize for.

00:34:10.113 --> 00:34:12.395
You've given me everything.

00:34:15.260 --> 00:34:16.427
Ready to go, kiddo?

00:34:16.449 --> 00:34:17.697
Yeah.

00:34:18.322 --> 00:34:20.555
Tyler, you're sure
Maggie's not around anymore?

00:34:20.613 --> 00:34:22.515
I'm sure. I'd see her.

00:34:27.970 --> 00:34:30.306
I guess whatever's
going on must be over.

00:34:35.483 --> 00:34:37.606
You two take care of
yourselves, all right?

00:34:42.060 --> 00:34:43.386
Thank you.

00:34:43.922 --> 00:34:44.927
Yeah.

00:34:44.932 --> 00:34:46.306
Both of you.

00:34:55.770 --> 00:34:58.346
Think you could have hooked
up some milf action there, bud.

00:34:58.350 --> 00:35:00.306
Serious, I think she liked you. Yeah,

00:35:00.322 --> 00:35:01.855
That's all she needs.

00:35:01.942 --> 00:35:04.108
Well, you saved the
mommy, you saved the girl.

00:35:04.109 --> 00:35:05.404
Not a bad day.

00:35:05.511 --> 00:35:07.257
'Course,you know, I could
have saved them myself,

00:35:07.340 --> 00:35:09.006
But I didn't want you to feel useless.

00:35:09.432 --> 00:35:11.025
All right, I appreciate it.

00:35:11.750 --> 00:35:13.985
Feels good getting back
in the saddle, doesn't it?

00:35:15.271 --> 00:35:16.234
Yeah.

00:35:17.072 --> 00:35:18.444
Yeah, it does.

00:35:18.471 --> 00:35:21.164
But it doesn't change what we
talked about last night, Dean.

00:35:22.751 --> 00:35:24.728
We talked about a lot
of things last night.

00:35:25.579 --> 00:35:27.395
You know what I mean. You were wasted.

00:35:27.502 --> 00:35:28.385
But you weren't...

00:35:29.512 --> 00:35:31.024
And you promised.



00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
